experiment: ctxgrid
  NOT power-gated: awake for all 2800 ticks of every trial (duty 1.000).
  This is the configuration that reproduces this experiment's banked
  numbers; a non-zero kCGDutyAwakeEnd freezes the creature after that tick.
  instrument        ctxgrid   trial seed 000000000135e1d4   2428 trials
                    another probe is another trial sequence: its numbers
                    are not comparable with these (~0.05 at 300 trials)
  the question      ctxfour got `nearest` at CHANCE on four words with a
                    PERFECT index. Was that a vocabulary ceiling, or a
                    vocabulary laid along ONE axis?
  the change        the same experiment with the words moved: a 2x2 of
                    two F1 levels x two F2 levels, all inside the
                    MEASURED reach, instead of kWords' vowel corners
                    where /i/ and /u/ sit 30 Hz apart on F1.
  the gate, folded in   F2 spread is the one number still projected.
                    This run measures it. Near-zero F2 spread with a
                    healthy F1 spread voids the naming claim and IS the
                    finding: reward reaching group 2 and not group 3.

  GUARD  every target inside the measured reach (F1 630+/-59, F2 1667+/-150)?  OK

