  FOUR-WORD NAMING WORKS, ON BOTH AXES. Against its OWN no-index
  control the 2x2 grid buys +0.157 of `nearest` (5.5 SE), with BOTH
  axes contributing: F1 +0.122 and F2 +0.127. ctxfour's same contrast on
  vowel-corner words is +0.118, so the LAYOUT is not what did it --
  both layouts name and the difference is not significant.

  AND IT CORRECTS ctxfour's VERDICT AS WELL AS ITS LAYOUT. That run read
  its oracle at 0.279 against 0.250 and called it chance, while its own
  off arm sat at 0.161 -- so its oracle beat its control too. Both runs
  were scored against a null their own tables contradicted.
